      "side": 1,
      "message": "@mihir.shah@rakuten.com We intentionally scoped this patch to parent-directory namespace operations because NFS clients have no wire operation to fsync a directory, whereas file state can be flushed by the client via fsync()/COMMIT. Also, vfs_open2() calls vfs_setattr2() internally during file creation, so adding fsync() inside vfs_setattr2() would add a second flush to file creates and slow down timestamp updates. If standalone SETATTR durability is needed, we can evaluate that in a separate follow-up patch.",
